        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x) = \\sin{x}.]</span> Calculate the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)]</span> about <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Let [MATH: f(x) = \\sin{x}.] Calculate the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)]</span> about <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x=a]</span> is given by</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: P_4(x) = f(a) + f&#x27;(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f&#x27;&#x27;(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\dfrac{f&#x27;&#x27;&#x27;(a)}{3!}(x-a)^3 + \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^4.]</span></p><p>Here, we have <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},]</span> so</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= f((\u03c0)/(2)) + f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2)) + (f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2}; + (f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(3!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{3} + (f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]</span></p><p>So we need to work out <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),]</span> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f&#x27;\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),]</span> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f&#x27;&#x27;\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),]</span> <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f&#x27;&#x27;&#x27;\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: f^{(4)}\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: f(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1; f^{\u2032}(x)|= \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{\u2033}(x)|= \u2212 \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2))|= \u2212 1; f^{\u2034}(x)|= \u2212 \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{(4)}(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1.]</span></p><p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: P_4(x)]</span> is given by</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= 1 \u2212 (1)/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}; = 1 \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(24)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=a] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_4(x) = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f''(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\dfrac{f'''(a)}{3!}(x-a)^3 + \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^4.]\n\nHere, we have [MATH: a=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},] so\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= f((\u03c0)/(2)) + f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2)) + (f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2}; + (f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(3!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{3} + (f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]\n\nSo we need to work out [MATH: f\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)] and [MATH: f^{(4)}\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] as follows:\n\n[MATH: f(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1; f^{\u2032}(x)|= \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{\u2033}(x)|= \u2212 \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2))|= \u2212 1; f^{\u2034}(x)|= \u2212 \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{(4)}(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1.]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: P_4(x)] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= 1 \u2212 (1)/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}; = 1 \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(24)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nLet [MATH: f(x) = \\sin{x}.] Calculate the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=a] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_4(x) = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f''(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\dfrac{f'''(a)}{3!}(x-a)^3 + \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^4.]\n\nHere, we have [MATH: a=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},] so\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= f((\u03c0)/(2)) + f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2)) + (f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2}; + (f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(3!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{3} + (f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]\n\nSo we need to work out [MATH: f\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)] and [MATH: f^{(4)}\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] as follows:\n\n[MATH: f(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1; f^{\u2032}(x)|= \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{\u2033}(x)|= \u2212 \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2))|= \u2212 1; f^{\u2034}(x)|= \u2212 \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{(4)}(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1.]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: P_4(x)] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= 1 \u2212 (1)/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}; = 1 \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(24)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]"
      },
