    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nThe [MATH: n]th-degree Taylor polynomial of a function [MATH: f(x)] around the point [MATH: x=a] is\n\nContent:\n[MATH: P_n(x) = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f''(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\cdots + \\dfrac{f^{(n)}(a)}{n!}(x-a)^n.]\n\nContent:\nIn particular, the coefficient of the [MATH: k]th-degree term is\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\dfrac{f^{(k)}(a)}{k!}.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Computing a Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial Of a Given Function About a Given Point\n\nExample Prompt:\nLet [MATH: f(x) = \\sin{x}.] Calculate the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=a] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_4(x) = f(a) + f'(a)(x-a) + \\dfrac{f''(a)}{2!}(x-a)^2 + \\dfrac{f'''(a)}{3!}(x-a)^3 + \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^4.]\n\nHere, we have [MATH: a=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2},] so\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= f((\u03c0)/(2)) + f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2)) + (f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2}; + (f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(3!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{3} + (f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2)))/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]\n\nSo we need to work out [MATH: f\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] [MATH: f'''\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right)] and [MATH: f^{(4)}\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\right),] as follows:\n\n[MATH: f(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1; f^{\u2032}(x)|= \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2032}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{\u2033}(x)|= \u2212 \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{\u2033}((\u03c0)/(2))|= \u2212 1; f^{\u2034}(x)|= \u2212 \\cos x|\u27f9|f^{\u2034}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 0; f^{(4)}(x)|= \\sin x|\u27f9|f^{(4)}((\u03c0)/(2))|= 1.]\n\nTherefore, [MATH: P_4(x)] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x)|= 1 \u2212 (1)/(2!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(4!)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}; = 1 \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{2} + (1)/(24)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(2))^{4}.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nFind the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: \\sin (3x)] about [MATH: x = (\u03c0)/(6).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3 + (9)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{2} + (27)/(4)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{4}]\nb. [MATH: 3 \u2212 (3)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6)) + (9)/(4)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{4}]\nc. [MATH: 1 \u2212 (9)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{2} + (27)/(8)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{4}]\nd. [MATH: 1 + (9)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{2} + (9)/(8)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{4}]\ne. [MATH: 1 \u2212 (3)/(2)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{2} + (9)/(4)(x \u2212 (\u03c0)/(6))^{4}]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nFind the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: \\ln x] about [MATH: x = 1.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x \u2212 1) \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 1)^{2} + (1)/(8)(x \u2212 1)^{3} \u2212 (1)/(24)(x \u2212 1)^{4}]\nb. [MATH: (x \u2212 1) \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 1)^{2} + (1)/(4)(x \u2212 1)^{3} \u2212 (1)/(8)(x \u2212 1)^{4}]\nc. [MATH: (x \u2212 1) \u2212 (1)/(3)(x \u2212 1)^{2} + (1)/(9)(x \u2212 1)^{3} \u2212 (1)/(27)(x \u2212 1)^{4}]\nd. [MATH: (x \u2212 1) \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 1)^{2} + (1)/(6)(x \u2212 1)^{3} \u2212 (1)/(24)(x \u2212 1)^{4}]\ne. [MATH: (x \u2212 1) \u2212 (1)/(2)(x \u2212 1)^{2} + (1)/(3)(x \u2212 1)^{3} \u2212 (1)/(4)(x \u2212 1)^{4}]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Obtaining a Higher-Order Derivative Of a Function Given its Higher-Degree Taylor Polynomial\n\nExample Prompt:\nThe fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x=0] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_4(x) = 1+2x-3x^2+4x^3-5x^4.]\n\nWhat is [MATH: f^{(4)}(0)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nThe coefficient of [MATH: x^4] is given by [MATH: \\dfrac{f^{(4)}(0)}{4!}.] Therefore,\n\n[MATH: (f^{(4)}(0))/(4!)|= \u2212 5; (f^{(4)}(0))/(24)|= \u2212 5; f^{(4)}(0)|= \u2212 120.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nThe fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x = 0] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_{4}(x) = 1 + 3x + (9)/(2)x^{2} \u2212 (9)/(2)x^{3} + (27)/(8)x^{4}.]\n\nWhat is [MATH: f^{\u2034}(0)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 18]\nb. [MATH: \u2212 27]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 (9)/(2)]\nd. [MATH: (9)/(4)]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 9]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nThe fifth-degree Taylor polynomial of [MATH: f(x)] about [MATH: x = 1] is given by\n\n[MATH: P_{5}(x) = 6 + 12(x \u2212 1) + 9(x \u2212 1)^{2} + 4(x \u2212 1)^{3} + (5)/(4)(x \u2212 1)^{4} + (3)/(10)(x \u2212 1)^{5}.]\n\nWhat is [MATH: f^{(5)}(1)?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 120]\nb. [MATH: 150]\nc. [MATH: 36]\nd. [MATH: 18]\ne. [MATH: 72]"
